{
  "name": "Onboard Stripe buyers into a Discord role with Postgres and Resend",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Onboard Stripe buyers into a Discord role\nGives everyone who buys a digital product a personal link to a buyers-only Discord role, and takes the role back on refund or dispute. Works with **Discord access claim**, **Remind buyers to claim Discord access** and **Error alerts**.\n\n### How it works\n1. Stripe sends `payment_intent.succeeded`. The trigger checks the Stripe signature.\n2. Only payments whose `metadata.productSlug` matches **Config** continue.\n3. The checkout session gives the buyer's email and name.\n4. The buyer is saved in Postgres. A unique key on the payment intent makes Stripe's retries harmless. A one-time claim token is created; only its SHA-256 is stored.\n5. Resend sends a welcome email with the personal claim link. An idempotency key blocks duplicate emails.\n6. A private Discord channel gets a sale alert.\n\nA full refund or a dispute marks the buyer and removes the Discord role.\n\n### Setup\n- Run **Setup: create the buyers table** once.\n- Credentials: Stripe (restricted key: Webhook Endpoints write, Checkout Sessions read), Postgres (`onboarding` database), Resend as Header Auth (`Authorization` = `Bearer re_...`), Discord Bot.\n- Fill in **Config**.\n- In workflow settings, set **Error alerts** as the error workflow.",
        "height": 760,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 1
      },
      "id": "55166750-b58b-4e73-83dd-618a6f6fa683",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -560,
        -120
      ]
    },
